.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
data/
# `outputs/model_metrics.json` ships with the model it describes. Excluding the whole
# directory was correct while the plan was to train after deploy; once the fitted model
# started shipping in the image, the metrics that go with it had to as well - otherwise
# `GET /model/metrics` answers 404 "Train the engine first" for the life of the release
# and the forecast page shows a failed request it can never recover from.
#
# The predictions dump stays out: 300 KB no route ever serves.
outputs/test_predictions.csv
# `artifacts/` is deliberately NOT excluded: the fitted model ships in the image so a
# release carries a known-good bundle. Excluding it was correct while the plan was to
# mount a volume and train after deploy.
*.md
.git
